# __NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

Generated from [`@provin-line/create-auth-provider`](https://github.com/provin-line/auth/tree/main/packages/create-auth-provider).
It wraps [`@o3co/auth-provider-core`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@o3co/auth-provider-core)
with the dPLaaX composition layer from
[`@provin-line/auth-provider-dplaax-module`](https://github.com/provin-line/auth/tree/main/packages/auth-provider-dplaax-module)
preregistered (DID grant resolver, JWT key store, client + code repositories,
HOCON config schema).

## Quick start

```bash
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ install
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run build
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run start
```

The service listens on `http://localhost:__PORT__` by default. Override
with `HTTP_PORT`. The DID registry the JWT-grant resolver queries is
`__REGISTRY_BASE_URL__`; override with `DPLAAX_REGISTRY_BASE_URL`.

Run the test suite:

```bash
__PACKAGE_MANAGER_BIN__ run test
```

## Configure

| Where | What |
| --- | --- |
| `config/application.conf` | HOCON for HTTP, JWT signing, OAuth grants, repositories, dplaax.registry. |
| `config/development.conf` / `config/production.conf` | Per-environment overlays merged via HOCON `withFallback`. |
| `config/clients.yaml` | OAuth client registry. Replace `example-client` with your real entries. |
| `keys/` | Signing-key material (`*.pem` / `*.key`). Globally gitignored. |

JWT signing defaults to EdDSA. Supply keys via `OAUTH_JWT_PRIVATE_KEY` /
`OAUTH_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY` env vars (or `*_PATH` variants pointing into
`keys/`), or flip `OAUTH_JWT_ALGORITHM` to `HS256` for symmetric signing.

## DID resolution

dPLaaX auth.provider accepts only **owner DIDs** as authentication
subjects (per spec § 2). Pipeline/process DIDs are handled by the Signer
API downstream and rejected by this resolver. The DID registry hostname
must match `dplaax.registry.baseUrl` (or be added to
`dplaax.registry.allowedRegistries` for migration scenarios).

## Docker

```bash
make docker                # build runtime image
make docker-compose-up     # local stack via docker-compose.yml
```

## Package manager

This scaffold uses pnpm (see `packageManager` in `package.json`) because
the dPLaaX module deps are pinned via pnpm's git-subdirectory syntax,
which is not npm-compatible. Override at your own risk.

